\section{Errors}{
 A run that cannot proceed gives an error of class
\code{mixedcheck_error}, whose element \code{issues} holds one issue: E7008 for a
family that is not accepted, E7009 for an access at T1 or T2 without a
valid reason, at T2 without the exploratory mode or with a formula
without a response, E1311 for a key of the wrong form, E1312 when no
secure source of random bytes is available to create one, the error of
\code{\link[=validate_declaration]{validate_declaration()}} or \code{\link[=read_table]{read_table()}}, E5012 for a value of a data
frame that is not one of the declared categories of its field, whether
or not the formula reads its column, E5011 for a column that the
declaration names and the data lack, the error of \code{\link[=formula_ir]{formula_ir()}}, E6069
for a predictor, grouping variable, offset, weights column, sample
column, column of the observation key, column of a declared unit or
assigned column that is the response, holds its trials or is declared an
outcome or derived from one, E7007 for a design sample, or at T1 and T2 an
analysis sample, without rows, and the errors of \code{\link[=design_matrices]{design_matrices()}} for
the values that the samples read. Arguments of the wrong type, a reason
at T0, an \code{outcome_seen} that differs from the declaration, columns of
other types, such as dates, and an invalid MIXEDCHECK_TIME give an
ordinary error. A plan that is not valid gives the error of
\code{\link[=validate_plan]{validate_plan()}}, and a run that does not belong to its plan E7310.
